<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Parris Island</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Parris Island is an island near Beaufort in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-carolina">South Carolina</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. It was the site of the French Huguenot outpost of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlesfort">Charlesfort</a>, built in 1562, and of the Spanish town of Santa Elena, capital of Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> for much of the period from 1566 to 1587. Since 1915 it has housed a major <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states-marine-corps">United States Marine Corps</a> recruit training depot.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/parris-island.jpg" alt="Parris Island" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marine_Corps_Recruit_Depot,_Parris_Island_logo-modified.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
